<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ager Faliscus</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Faliscan territory</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ager Faliscus was the territory of the Falisci, an Italic people of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/etruria">Etruria</a> living north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tiber-river">Tiber</a> and the Monti Cimini. The Falisci spoke Faliscan, a language closely related to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a>, but shared much of their material culture with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/etruscans">Etruscans</a>. Their chief town was Falerii, and the region came fully under Roman control after Rome crushed a Faliscan revolt in 241 BCE.</p></div>
